## Open questions

Every requirement row gets one pass asking what it does **not** say: which
state, which permutation, which pre-existing user choice. Send the whole list
to the requirement owner in one batch before the first commit.

An unanswered question does not block the loop — it must instead be recorded as
`assumed:`, so the assumption ships visibly in the PR rather than surfacing on
staging.

| id | question | asked | resolution |
|----|----------|-------|------------|
| Q-1 | Does the modal appear when the user already chose "no replacement"? | 2026-08-13 | answered: no — suppress it entirely |
| Q-2 | What does the badge show at zero markup? | 2026-08-13 | assumed: hide the badge; flagged in PR body |

---

## Permutation matrix

The axes this feature has to survive, enumerated once, up front. A blank cell is
a defect waiting for QA to find it — every cell is covered or explicitly waived
with a reason.

Keep it to the axes that actually interact. Three axes with four values each is
a real matrix; ten axes is a wish list nobody fills in.

| id | cell | covered by |
|----|------|------------|
| M-1 | scenario 3 × copay × markup > 0 | spec: spec/services/replacement_spec.rb |
| M-2 | scenario 3 × copay × zero markup | spec: spec/services/replacement_spec.rb |
| M-3 | scenario 4 × subsidy × capture time passed | waived: capture time cannot be set in the past |

